  "notes": [
    "File contains two standalone procedures with no package declaration: Diag and Accumulate_One_Member.",
    "Diag (lines 1-5) is pure debug output via DBMS_OUTPUT; excluded as infrastructure.",
    "Accumulate_One_Member is a partially developed version of the full procedure. The crDues cursor loop is present (lines 144-175) with the M (Membership) row branch active. The E (Employment) and I (Irregular Service) row branches are not yet present.",
    "The vStDteFound flag initialisation on lines 105-108 is infrastructure setup with no active consumer in this version; excluded.",
    "The crBirthDate OPEN/FETCH/CLOSE on lines 114-116 retrieves vBirthDate, which is not referenced in the active M-row logic; excluded as setup for future E/I branch logic.",
    "Source defect: the Get_old_Dues call on line 132 is missing a trailing semicolon.",
    "The value '1' used as a sentinel for Calcs_Load.gCSSDuesID on line 131 does not appear to be a real Dues ID but an embedded signal value. Flagged for review.",
    "The loop exit on line 168 (EXIT WHEN vTermDate < vDueRec.Start_Date) is annotated in source as 'we've had a hiccup - exit abnormally' — an unexpected condition where the computed terminal date precedes the membership start date. Modelled as EXIT_LOOP (ACT-AOM-011B); does not exit the procedure."
  ],
